nodecode-mcp-serve is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
  commit e7a218f26db88426ab3e7376f0e000b6e356f5e7
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (LICENSE)

The rewrite reimplements the plugin's conversation bridge as one MCP route on
this Nodecode's own gateway port: the JSON-RPC handshake, `tools/list` and
`tools/call`, and six tools over Nodecode's own session directory and event
log (conversations_list, conversation_get, messages_read, events_poll,
messages_send, channels_list), with a `/mcp-serve` command that prints the
client configuration and a config section of its own. The original's
Python, its `state.db` SQLite reads and its messaging-platform plumbing are
gone: Nodecode's sessions are the conversations, `nlk:events` is the read
and `nle:submit` is the send. Left out because they have no Nodecode
counterpart in this cell's shape: the stdio transport (a client POSTs to the
route instead of launching a process), `attachments_fetch` and the two
approval tools, and `--tools`, which re-exported Hermes' own web, browser,
vision and speech tools to the connecting agent.
